<title>MEXICO: Mexico vehicle production up Jan-Sept on yr.</title>
<headline>Mexico vehicle production up Jan-Sept on yr.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's automobile industry produced 925,838 vehicles during the first nine months of the year versus 668,349 units produced during the same period of 1995, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Mexico also exported 740,684 units during the year's first nine months versus 545,890 during the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods. For last year figures are either numbers or percentages. Percentages are the variation in this year's first none months to the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>				   JAN-SEPT 96	    JAN-SEPT 95</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	     925,838		  668,349</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 181,668		  118,153</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   744,170		  +35.7 pct</p>
<p>		autos		  499,532		  +14.5 pct</p>
<p>		trucks and buses   244,638		 +114.9 pct</p>
<p>    TOTAL SALES		    948,397		  664,175</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 207,713		  118,285</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   740,684		  545,890</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES 206,955		  165,752</p>
<p>		autos		  125,219		  105,133</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    81,736		   60,619</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289530.</p>
